This folder contains all of the files necessary to replicate Nyhan and Montgomery (“Connecting the Candidates”). The files provided are described below.

*************
Top directory
*************

nyhan-montgomery.do

Provides the code necessary to replicate Table 1 in the main text.

nyhan-montgomery.R  

Provides the code necessary to replicate Figures 1-2 and Tables 2-4 in the main text as well as Tables 2-5 and Figure 3 in the supporting information.

**************
Data directory
**************
 
allCand-log-after-proj.dta 

The adjacency matrix using the logged dollar amounts for tie strength.       

allCand-shared-cons.dta  

The adjacency matrix used in the main text (number of shared consultants).

canddata-jd-names-d02.csv     

The names of the 2002 Democratic candidates in the Druckman et al. data for whom outcome data was not missing.

candidates-consultants-party.dta

The edge list of candidates and consultants who were included in the Druckman et al. data for whom outcome data was not missing.

CEDyads.csv	 

As described in the main text and supporting information, we checked the results of our coding of the FEC expenditures data against Campaigns & Elections scorecard data. This process helped us identify some dyads that had been inadvertently dropped in the data cleaning process or as a result of a coding error. All errors were subsequently redressed not only for these cases, but for any other cases that may have been affected by the errors. In essences, this stage aided us in identifying problems in our data cleaning method and other procedures that were subsequently corrected. 

However, Table SI-2 reports how our FEC data compares with C&E data at this stage as a point of comparison. This file is a complete listing of all dyads reported in this period for these candidates as reported in C&E. It also provides the name of the consulting firm, the candidate name, and the state and district for the candidate. The FailedToFind variable indicates whether or not the dyad was found in our FEC-based dataset at the outset and the ReasonNotFound variable codes the reason this case was missing. Codes for ReasonNotFound are as follows: 1=expenditure not included because term in expenditure data matched list of keywords to exclude; 2=candidate expenditure list was incorrectly excluded; 3=missing because of PAC name included keywords that were on list to exclude; 4="Correct" missingness; 5=missing for unknown reason; 6=RA error; 7=Conflict between RA coding incorrectly resolved by researcher. Only cases coded 4 were actually excluded from the final analysis. (The other codes were used to clean the data manually.)

consultcandmatrix-jd-d02.dta

The adjacency matrix of 2002 Democratic candidates and consultants who were included in the Druckman et al. data for whom outcome data was not missing.

canddata-jd-names-d02.csv     

The names of the consultants for 2002 Democratic candidates in the Druckman et al. data for whom outcome data was not missing.

MainRegressionData.csv  

This dataset provides the main outcome variables and covariates needed for our spatial regressions. 

partyyearpresSHARED, partyyearraceSHARED, regionpartyyearSHARED (subdirectories)

Each of these directories contains 500 randomly permuted adjacency matrices as outlines in the main text. These are used in the creation of Figure SI-3. We created three different types of permutations -- party/year/district favorability, party/year/region and party/year/incumbency status. An example of the code used to generate these matrices is shown in nyhan-montgomery.R. However, these are the actual randomly generated matrices needed to perfectly replicate the published results.

******************
dataPrep directory
******************

consulltantKeywords.csv

This file contains all of the keywords used to identify potential payments to consultants that were later checked by RA coders.

DataCleaningNotes.docx

This file contains a few explanations as to why certain terms were identified for exclusion below.

DeleteTheseCRPRecipname.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the CRPRecipname field, the entry was deleted. 

DeleteTheseDescrip.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the DESCRIP field, the entry was deleted. 

DeleteTheseEntType.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the EntType field, the entry was deleted. (See DataCleaningNotes)

DeleteTheseExpcode.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the Expcode field, the entry was deleted. (See DataCleaningNotes)

DeleteTheseRecipcode.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the Recipcode field, the entry was deleted. (See DataCleaningNotes)

DeleteThesePacshort.csv

The list of terms used to delete cases. If these terms appeared in the Pacshort field, the entry was deleted. (See DataCleaningNotes)
